fact WorkItem(id: "WI-244", description: some(value: "Consolidate anthill-core integration tests from 59 separate files into ~8 grouped binaries to slash per-binary linker overhead. Each integration test file today compiles into a standalone binary; linking takes ~50-100s on local hardware. Full integration sweep currently runs for hours (observed: ~52 minutes through 13/59 binaries during WI-243 testing). Proposed grouping: (a) wi_tests.rs — all wi### validation tests (wi009/071/182/186/202/204×2/205/210/211/218/219/221/222/223×3/224/226/227/228/230/231/236/237*), ~25 files; (b) eval_tests.rs — eval_test, eval_q3, eval_q4; (c) induction_tests.rs — induction_axiom_witness, induction_rule, numeric_induction, scope_axiom_witness, specialization_witness; (d) builtin_tests.rs — persistence, persistence_builtins, map_builtins, time_now, toml_ser, vec3_ops; (e) parse_tests.rs — parse, typing, cli_parse, codegen, fact_substitution; (f) algebra_tests.rs — algebra_spec, ring_polynom, logic_sorts, console_stdlib, operation_equation, equational_attr; (g) resolve_tests.rs — forall_impl_resolve, push_choice, route_dispatch, guard_trigger, nested_implication, proof_load, tactic_ir, incremental_load. Keep github_todo_test.rs standalone (large fixtures, distinct concern). Pattern: each consolidated file declares mod submodules referencing the original test files via #[path = '...'] mod foo, OR move test functions directly into the grouped file. Net: 59 → 8 binaries, ~85% fewer linker invocations. Risk LOW: rust's test harness isolates each #[test] fn within a binary; only watch-out is shared static / thread_local state which anthill tests avoid (load-fresh-KB-per-test pattern). Acceptance: cargo-test green; record before/after timing of full integration sweep in the deliver feedback (target: hours → single-digit minutes). Discovered during WI-243 testing where the long sweep blocked verification."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-15T15:24:05Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-244", author: "user", content: "Timing: full anthill-core test suite ran in 452s (7.5 min) after consolidation — was running for >2 hours pre-consolidation (incomplete sweep observed during WI-243). Per-binary linker/spawn overhead dropped from ~60 invocations to 9 (lib + 8 wrappers + doc-tests). Test execution time itself is only ~41s total across all binaries; the remaining ~390s of wall time is the irreducible per-binary linker setup (~45s × 9). Further reduction would require either merging all integration tests into one binary (loses the topic-grouped browsability) or using --no-default-features / release builds. Test count preserved: 204 lib + 632 integration = 836 total, all green.", at: "2026-05-15T15:24:05Z")
